### Research trail (why this is excluded)

1. Two web searches on 2026-10-27 ("Neomorph AI model LLM release benchmarks"; `"neomorph" huggingface OR openrouter OR "open weights" language model provider`) returned **zero** AI-model matches: no vendor announcement, no model card, no leaderboard entry, no provider listing, no benchmark table anywhere.
2. The name collisions found (biotech company, Instagram handle, SD UI theme) are the likely roster-contamination sources — the Instagram handle in particular comments on LLM-news posts, which can surface "neomorph" adjacent to model keywords in search indexes.
3. If the roster intended a different identity, the closest real candidates by name shape are **Neo**-prefixed models (e.g. Nous "Hermes"-family derivatives) or **Morph**-adjacent tooling (morphllm) — none of which are plausibly a single model named "Neomorph"; no mapping could be made responsibly.
4. Per contract: zero verified public benchmark numbers → `.md.excluded`, never invented numbers. The pre-existing `average.md` in this folder could not have come from a real `neomorph` evaluation and should be reviewed by the project owner.

